  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Shaun Roger White (born September 3, 1986) is an American former professional snowboarder and skateboarder. He is a five-time Olympian and a three-time Olympic gold medalist in half-pipe snowboarding. He holds the world record for the most X Games gold medals and most Olympic gold medals by a snowboarder. He has also won ten ESPY Awards throughout his career in various categories.\nOutside of his Olympic and skateboarding career White plays guitar in the band the Bad Things and started his own snowboarding league \"The Snow League\" in 2025.\n\n",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
